  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v4.2.8 - Rebuilt against SpawnDev.SpawnJS 2.1.17. 4.2.7 was compiled against SpawnJS 2.1.7, where FileSystemWritableFileStream.Seek and .Truncate took a ulong; 2.1.17 takes a long. The change is source-compatible, so every build of every consumer stayed green while the shipped IL still called the ulong overloads - the failure only appears at runtime, as MissingMethodException, and only on the code path that runs. Both call sites are on the real piece-write path (AsyncFSFileStore.WriteViewViaWritableAsync and GetWritableAsync), not only the OPFS layout probes, so any download taking the writable path threw. No API or behaviour change in this package: a recompile against the current SpawnJS is the entire fix. The two broken references were found by resolving every SpawnJS memberref in the shipped assembly against the assembly that actually loads, which is now a build gate (_tools/AbiCheck) rather than something a consumer discovers.",
